Changes made:

`src/types.ts:4` — added `"storehouse"` to the `BuildingKind` union.

`src/sim.ts` — four additions:
- Added `storehouse: { wood: 25, stone: 10 }` to `BUILDING_COSTS`.
- Added `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` (a `Record<BuildingKind, BuildingKind[]>`) with prerequisites for every kind: only `storehouse` requires `["hut"]`; `hut`/`farm`/`quarry` have none.
- Added `isAllowed(settlement, kind)` helper — a building is allowed iff all its prerequisite kinds are already in `settlement.buildings`.
- Added `availableBuildings(settlement)` returning every kind that is both `canAfford`ed and `isAllowed`.

Behavior: `availableBuildings` filters over all kinds in `BUILDING_COSTS` (so it stays in sync if more kinds are added), keeping only those the settlement can pay for and is permitted to build. A `storehouse` only appears when a `hut` is already present and the settlement has ≥25 wood and ≥10 stone; `hut`/`farm`/`quarry` are gated by affordability alone.


